{"agent":"fleet-ci-clone","data":{"body":"Fixes bug B81f52de542: tests/test_clone_id_recovery.py::test_newest_claim_wins_when_two_suffixes_qualify does next(iterdir()) over .ddflow/worktrees, which holds T1 AND a .gitignore file. On a filesystem listing .gitignore first (runner ext4) the planted lease records a non-directory as its worktree, _linked_tree_here rejects it, and the real claim's suffix wins: assert 'fb2ddd' == 'aaaaaa'. Fixture order bug, not Python-version specific; production logic is correct.\n\nWrite the regression test first and watch it FAIL on the unfixed code; then `ddflow complete fix-B81f52de542 --regression-test <test>` closes the bug with the task (or `ddflow bug fixed B81f52de542 --regression-test <test>` first).","fixes":["B81f52de542"],"globs":["tests/test_clone_id_recovery.py"],"line":"","needs":[],"older_ddflow":"0.2.4","parent":"","priority":10,"tags":["bugfix"],"title":"Fix bug B81f52de542: CI flake: test_newest_claim_wins picks .gitignore as the worktree (3.12 runner)"},"id":"e74ab69f3e21aac9c7340914c","kind":"task.added","lamport":87320,"schema":1,"subject":"fix-B81f52de542","ts":"2026-10-20T12:02:03.490434Z"}
